From: h713 <h713@local>
Date: Thu, 28 Aug 2026 18:10:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] EXPERIMENT: attach DECD to IOMMU master 2, as stock does at
 playback

This is the last unported step of stock's post-THal_Vp_Init resume, and it
pairs with 0068. On its own it does nothing: the `dec` node is disabled in
the production DT, so no platform device is created and no IOMMU attachment
happens. It only takes effect on an 0068 boot.

What stock actually does, recovered from board-B `ge2d_dev.ko`. HWC's SVP
resume path runs four operations after `THal_Vp_Init` returns, and three of
them we already have:

  powerCtrl(1)             /dev/ge2d ioctl 0x4680 -> __pm_runtime_resume(dev, 4)
                           i.e. pm_runtime_get_sync().  We have this as
                           DECD_IOC_PM_HINT; ioctl 0x4680 with a zero payload
                           is __pm_runtime_idle(dev, 4), our PM_HINT off.
  DecoderDisplay::enable(1)  /dev/decd enable -> our dec_enable().
  frame submit             /dev/decd DECD_IOC_FRAME_SUBMIT -> patch 0067.
  iommuEnable()            /dev/ge2d ioctl 0x4681 -> THIS, and only this,
                           was missing.

`0x4681` is four instructions and leaves no room for interpretation:

    92d0: mov  r1, #1
    92d4: mov  r0, #2
    92d8: bl   sunxi_enable_device_iommu     <- R_ARM_CALL relocation
    92dc: ldr  r8, [r4]
    92e0: b    <return>

So: master 2, translation on. Master 2 is `dec@5600000` -- this device's own
register window -- shared with `ge2d@5240000`. The stock DTB ships that master
as `<&mmu_aw 2 0>`, bypassing; stock turns translation *on* at runtime, when
HWC is about to present video. Our `dec` node has carried no `iommus` property
at all, so every DECD test so far has fetched untranslated physical addresses.
That is why the four-slot register file held `Y=0x6c500000` rather than an
IOVA.

`video_buffer_map()` already does the right thing either way: it attaches the
dma-buf to this device and takes `sg_dma_address()`, which becomes an IOVA once
the device is translated. No driver change is needed for the addresses.

WHY THIS IS OUT OF SERIES, and the hazard to expect.

Master 2 is shared with the live display. On an 0068 boot the panel is still
showing U-Boot's logo, fetched by the AFBD hardware from the physical carveout
at 0x6c100000 through this same master. Translating master 2 while that fetch
is in flight makes it fault: the adopted scanout has no mapping. Patch 0051
keeps that a rate-limited log line rather than a hang, but the logo may go
away the moment the device attaches.

For this experiment that is tolerable and arguably wanted -- the DECD tests
already hide the logo channel deliberately, and the open question is whether
DECD output ever reaches the panel. But it is a real departure from the
adopted-display model the rest of the tree is built on, where Linux never
disturbs what U-Boot left running. Do not put this in series on the strength
of "stock does it": stock owns composition from the ground up and never adopts
a foreign scanout, so it never has a live untranslated fetch to break.

The prediction worth recording before the run: if DECD frames become visible
only with this applied, the missing piece was address translation and the
firmware/hardware was discarding untranslated fetches. If the panel goes black
at attach and stays black, this tells us master 2 is genuinely shared and the
adopted display cannot coexist with a translated DECD -- which would mean the
no-GPU route needs Linux to own the whole display, not adopt it.

RUN ON HARDWARE 2026-08-28. The second branch happened, and the run is
CONFOUNDED -- it says nothing about DECD routing. Do not cite it as a negative
for the no-GPU path.

Boot sequence, operator watching: U-Boot logo appears, then goes black and
stays black. One fault, at attach:

  platform 5600000.dec: Adding to iommu group 0
  sun50i-iommu 2010000.iommu: Page fault for 0x000000006c332000 (master 2, dir rd)

0x6c332000 is inside U-Boot's logo carveout at 0x6c100000. So master 2 really
is the display's own fetch path, and translating it invalidates the adopted
scanout's physical source address immediately.

What this patch DOES achieve, and it is worth keeping: the iommuEnable port is
mechanically correct. With a frame held, DECD queued proper IOVAs --

  0x05600070 = 0xFFC00000   Y
  0x05600084 = 0xFFCE1000   C, delta 0xE1000 = one 1280x720 luma plane

-- and fetched them at 60 IRQ/s with ZERO further page faults and zero
panfrost GPU/MMU/job interrupts. Translation works; DECD is happy behind it.

Why the run is confounded. The panel was black, but a positive control failed:
the live OSD channel was repointed at DECD's own IOVA (0x05600178 = 0xFFC00000)
and its READY latch was consumed (0x05600144 -> 0), with no page fault -- and
the panel stayed black anyway. A channel fetching a valid, mapped, populated
buffer rendered nothing. Meanwhile vsync stayed at 59.7 Hz (16.75 ms deltas)
and the latch kept being consumed, so the timing generator and commit logic
were alive the whole time.

The reading is that ONE translation fault wedges the AFBD fetch engine for the
rest of the boot. Latch consumption and vsync prove the commit path, not the
fetch path. So nothing could have appeared on this boot regardless of DECD
routing, and the black screen carries no information about it.

The fix that would make this experiment valid is concrete: map the display
carveout into the same IOMMU domain so the adopted scanout survives
translation -- an identity mapping for 0x6c100000, via a reserved-memory region
with iommu-addresses, or by having the driver map it at attach. Until the
adopted scanout can fetch under translation, master 2 cannot be translated on a
display Linux inherited rather than programmed.

Signed-off-by: Christopher Stenger <chris.h.stenger@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h713.dtsi
@@ -1663,6 +1663,21 @@
 			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_DISP>;
 			reset-names = "rst_bus_disp";
 			memory-region = <&decd_reserved>;
+			/*
+			 * Master 2, translation on -- the port of stock's
+			 * /dev/ge2d ioctl 0x4681, which is exactly
+			 * sunxi_enable_device_iommu(2, 1) and runs in HWC's
+			 * SVP resume just before the first video frame.
+			 *
+			 * The stock DTB ships this master bypassing
+			 * (`<&mmu_aw 2 0>`) and flips it at runtime. Master 2
+			 * is shared with ge2d@5240000 and with whatever is
+			 * already scanning out, so on an adopted U-Boot
+			 * display this will fault the logo fetch. Inert in the
+			 * production DT, where this node is disabled; only an
+			 * 0068 boot creates the device.
+			 */
+			iommus = <&iommu 2 1>;
 			/*
 			 * 100 MHz, not the vendor's 200: dec_enable() does
 			 * clk_set_rate(clk_afbd, this) on runtime resume, and
